>
> "weil'nd" isn't Lojban; the letter "w" is not used, and "'" can occur only
> between two vowels. I don't see anything else wrong with it, without seeing
> the original.
>
> Pierre
> --
> li ze te'a ci vu'u ci bi'e te'a mu du
> li ci su'i ze te'a mu bi'e vu'u ci


To get "Francis Weiland Thurston", I suggest {la.fransis.ueiland.turston.}
or {la francis.ueilynd.turston.} If you place a {.} at the beginning of the
name, you can have {la} in it, otherwise, I think {ly} is the closest
allowable sound.


